{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>For he flatters</b> — from the stem of <i>its words are smooth</i> [החליקה], as in <i>but I am a smooth man</i>. <b>For he flatters</b> [כי החליק]: the matter is evil in his eyes, to find HaShem his iniquity, and he hates Him, after the manner of <i>may Elohim find the iniquity of your servants</i>. \n\nThe verse cited is Genesis 44:16, the same root appearing in Judges 5:6, 12:8."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:46.305576091Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}